---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import Split from '@/components/ui/Split.astro';
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button.astro';
import Strata from '@/components/art/Strata.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '@/components/seo/schema';
import { principles } from '@/data/principles';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="The purpose, perspective and founder behind Tarvanta, an insights-led platform for understanding meaningful problems and developing enduring ventures."
  schema={breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'About', path: '/about/' }])}
>
  <PageHero
    page="About"
    statement="Good ideas deserve more than a quick start."
    lede="Tarvanta is being built around a simple conviction: meaningful problems deserve careful attention, and worthwhile ideas deserve the discipline to become something useful."
  />

  <div class="h-40 md:h-56" aria-hidden="true">
    <Strata stems={[0.78]} seed={5} layers={11} />
  </div>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="why-title">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <Split>
        <h2 slot="heading" id="why-title" class="t-heading max-w-[14ch]">Why Tarvanta exists</h2>
        <div class="prose-body">
          <p>
            Many business conversations begin with a proposed solution. The more useful starting
            point is often the question that came before it: what is not working, for whom, and why
            has it remained unresolved?
          </p>
          <p>
            Tarvanta is an insights-led global venture platform intended to connect that first
            investigation with practical development. It is not tied to one sector, product or
            service. Its focus is the quality of the problem, the strength of the evidence and the
            usefulness of the response.
          </p>
          <p>
            A sound response may become an independent venture. It may also be a product, a
            partnership, a different operating model or a decision to leave an idea unbuilt.
          </p>
        </div>
      </Split>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section border-t border-stone" aria-labelledby="purpose-title">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <Split>
        <h2 slot="heading" id="purpose-title" class="t-heading max-w-[14ch]">Purpose and ambition</h2>
        <div class="prose-body">
          <p class="t-lede text-charcoal">
            To turn well-understood problems into considered action, and to build ventures only
            where the case is strong enough.
          </p>
          <p>
            Tarvanta's ambition is international, with an Indian perspective and an open view of
            where useful ideas can originate. The platform is designed to connect insight with
            execution, while allowing future ventures to develop their own identities and serve
            their own markets.
          </p>
          <p>
            Its wider purpose is to use the knowledge, relationships and capacity developed through
            responsible growth to contribute to worthwhile causes. That is an ambition to work
            towards, not a claim of an established impact programme.
          </p>
        </div>
      </Split>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="on-dark bg-charcoal text-ink-on-dark" aria-labelledby="operating-title">
    <div class="page-wrap section">
      <Split>
        <h2 slot="heading" id="operating-title" class="t-heading max-w-[14ch] text-paper">
          How the platform is designed to operate
        </h2>
        <div class="prose-body">
          <p class="text-ink-on-dark">
            Tarvanta is intended to hold the work that benefits from continuity: research,
            strategic thinking, standards and long-term direction. Independent ventures should
            retain what needs to belong to them: their name, brand, product, voice and customer
            relationships.
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-on-dark">
            This separation is deliberate. It gives each venture room to respond to its market
            without losing the benefit of a shared foundation.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/approach/" class="link">See the approach stage by stage</a></p>
        </div>
      </Split>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
    <div class="page-wrap grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-8">
      <div class="md:col-span-4">
        <p class="t-label">The founder</p>
        <h2 id="founder-title" class="t-heading mt-4 max-w-[12ch]">Lalit Yadav</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose-body md:col-span-7 md:col-start-6">
        <p class="t-lede text-charcoal">
          Tarvanta was founded by Lalit Yadav, whose professional background brings together
          business presentation, visual communication and the discipline of making complex ideas
          clear.
        </p>
        <p>
          His documented experience includes working as a Business Presentation Specialist at
          McKinsey &amp; Company in Bengaluru and as a Senior Presentations Associate with Williams
          Lea in London. He has also worked across customer support, marketing and corporate
          communications.
        </p>
        <p>
          Lalit studied digital marketing at the University of Salford, including a semester
          exchange at the Berlin School of Economics and Law, and holds a BBA in Marketing from
          Alliance University.
        </p>
        <p>
          That background informs an important principle at Tarvanta: sound thinking should be
          understandable. Evidence, analysis and decisions are only useful when they can be
          communicated with accuracy and purpose.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lalit-presentationspecialist/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Connect with Lalit on LinkedIn
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section border-t border-stone bg-paper" aria-labelledby="values-title">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <div class="max-w-[38rem]">
        <h2 id="values-title" class="t-heading">Principles that guide the work</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-graphite">
          These are the standards Tarvanta intends to apply, including when the evidence argues
          against an idea.
        </p>
      </div>
      <dl class="mt-14 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-12 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:mt-20 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {principles.map((p) => (
          <div class="border-t border-charcoal pt-6">
            <dt class="t-subheading">{p.title}</dt>
            <dd class="mt-3 text-graphite">{p.body}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="next-title">
    <div class="page-wrap flex flex-col gap-8 md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between">
      <h2 id="next-title" class="t-heading max-w-[20ch]">A thoughtful question is a good place to begin.</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-5">
        <Button href="/approach/">Our approach</Button>
        <Button href="/contact/" variant="quiet">Start a conversation</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
